---
import Frame from '../../components/PageFrame.astro';
const items = [
  {
    title: 'Searchable sample documents',
    body: 'Search titles, excerpts and categories across six original local documents.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Clear sources',
    body: 'Open a result and inspect its fictional handbook or playbook reference before acting.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Empty states that help',
    body: 'Understand when nothing matches, clear the filters and begin again without losing your place.',
  },
];
---

<Frame label="Knowledge" items={items}>
  <section class="container section demo-section" id="demo-guide">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">TRY IT / SAMPLE LIBRARY</p>
      <h2>Find the guidance. Check the source.</h2>
      <p>
        Try “onboarding”, “review” or “scope”. Combine a search with Guides,
        Projects or Policies. Open a result to read the excerpt. These are
        prepared samples, with no connected company documents or AI-generated
        answers.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section split-section">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">MORE THAN A RESULT</p>
      <h2>A useful answer has somewhere to come from.</h2>
      <p>
        A title helps you recognise the subject. An excerpt helps you judge
        relevance. A reference tells you where to check the original context.
        Together they support a more informed next step.
      </p>
      <p>
        Search does not decide which policy applies to a real situation. The
        person reading still needs to assess its scope and whether the source is
        current.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="reading">
      <h3>Organise a library people can use</h3>
      <p>
        Choose specific titles, define a few recognisable categories and give
        each document an owner. Record when it was reviewed. Retire obsolete
        guidance rather than letting conflicting copies compete.
      </p>
      <h3>Protect the boundary</h3>
      <p>
        This example has no uploads, accounts or remote query service. Search
        text is compared locally and is not sent to an analytics provider. Use
        sample terms; never paste private company material into a public
        demonstration.
      </p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/guides/#privacy">
        Read the privacy boundaries →
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container section">
    <img
      class="diagram"
      src="/images/diagrams/knowledge-flow.svg"
      width="1200"
      height="340"
      loading="lazy"
      alt="Illustrative sequence: question, search library, read sources, next action."
    />
    <p class="demo-note">
      The diagram describes the local example: you search a fixed library and
      inspect prepared text. No external service is connected.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/products/workflows/">
      See the approval example those documents support →
    </a>
  </section>
</Frame>
